feat: methodology page + track record section (credibility sprint)

Two new pieces of the audit's Sprint 3 credibility block.

1. /methodology page documents the scoring algorithm in full:
   - The 6 signals with their exact weights, thresholds, and formulas
   - Cross-cutting override rules (low-velocity caps, deprecation bumps)
   - Risk classification table
   - Data sources (GitHub REST via Octokit, npm registry)
   - Refresh cadence per route (scan / is-maintained / weekly reports)
   - Link to the open-source scoring code at lib/scoring.ts

2. TrackRecord section on the landing page (between ComparisonSection and
   HowItWorks) shows 6 historic packages with their decline pattern:
   moment, request, bower, node-sass, underscore, coffeescript. Phrasing
   is honest about the pattern recognition (not fabricated retroactive
   scores).

Wiring:
- Footer gets text links to methodology, vs Snyk Advisor, weekly reports
  next to the GitHub/Email icons
- ScoringGrid gets a "Read the full methodology" CTA under the cards
- sitemap.ts includes /methodology

